From 4197761dae6938730f948ac596026c26b145a6cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:56:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] feat(llms): route Bedrock Mantle models through SigV4
 createBedrockMantle

Amazon Bedrock serves some models only on the OpenAI-compatible Mantle
endpoint (bedrock-mantle.<region>.api.aws), for example Grok 4.3, Gemma 4
and the bare openai.gpt-5.x ids, and serves others on Mantle in Regions
where bedrock-runtime lacks them. The Bedrock vendor only created a
Converse client, so these models failed, and the only workaround was a
generic OpenAI provider with a 12-hour Bedrock API key.

The Bedrock vendor now routes a model to Mantle when its id carries the
`aws-mantle/` prefix or its catalog entry declares an OpenAI wire
protocol. The models.dev normalizer maps `@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock/mantle`
to `openai-responses`, so the next catalog refresh flags the Mantle-only
models automatically. Everything else, including inference profiles and
ARNs, stays on Converse.

- Credentials: Mantle reuses the Converse credential decision. IAM and
  profile auth sign with SigV4 (service bedrock-mantle) through the same
  fromNodeProviderChain provider, including credential_process, and
  suppress the AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK fallback. API-key auth still
  sends the configured key.
- Endpoint: https://bedrock-mantle.<region>.api.aws for the resolved
  Region (options.region, AWS_REGION, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION). Mantle serves
  each model on one of two routes and rejects the other with HTTP 400
  "isn't supported on this route": GPT-5 and later, Grok and Gemma 4 use
  /openai/v1, everything else (gpt-oss, Gemma 3, Qwen, DeepSeek, GLM,
  Kimi, MiniMax, Mistral) uses /v1, per the AWS model cards and a live
  probe of all 49 us-west-2 and 50 us-east-2 Mantle models. The vendor
  picks the documented route first and, on a route rejection, retries
  once on the other route and remembers it for the provider module. The
  bedrock-runtime endpoint override is never reused; aws.mantleEndpoint
  sets a Mantle base URL (for example a VPC endpoint) that is used as-is.
  A missing Region fails with an actionable error.
- API: Chat Completions by default (widest Mantle coverage), Responses
  when the catalog says so or aws.mantleApi is "responses".
- Parameters: temperature is sent only to Mantle models whose catalog
  entry declares it. OpenAI reasoning ids behind the `openai.` vendor
  prefix get forceReasoning, so the SDK sends max_completion_tokens and
  no sampling parameters.
- Settings: aws.mantleEndpoint and aws.mantleApi flow from provider
  settings to gateway options.

Tests: 25 new vendor tests (routing, credentials, Region, route
selection and fallback, parameters), 5 wire tests through the real
@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock/mantle package with a stubbed fetch (URL, SigV4
Authorization scope, body, route retry), 1 catalog normalizer test, 3
settings plumbing tests.
